      "title": "Modeling Inhibited Growth"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "bb3f4bbe-d0c1-57f7-b4ee-9f454dd4775c",
      ":question/problem": "The growth of the number of deer in a protected forest is directly proportional to the difference between its maximum capacity and its current population. Let $N(t)$ be the number of deer, and let $t\\ge 0$ be the time in years. If the maximum capacity is $200$ deer, which differential equation models this population? Assume that $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "5582c0bc-fe9a-5d22-b375-8c4450a3a0a8",
          ":answer-field/key": "selection",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/radio",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "8eaa68da-41cb-5337-bed2-e4ddaf6f872d",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "\\frac{\\text{d}N}{\\text{d}t}=-k(200+N)"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "8e44e2a9-a947-5d7c-9e91-2bd901fed5d9",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "\\frac{\\text{d}N}{\\text{d}t}=kN(200-N)"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "f5295694-6b8f-5c12-87c2-00c0e0dd10b4",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "\\frac{\\text{d}N}{\\text{d}t}=k{N}^{2}(200-N)"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "1590d796-ddbb-5261-9314-57adf67575fa",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "\\frac{\\text{d}N}{\\text{d}t}=k(200-N)"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "d1e032db-0faf-5765-a379-9f1176679c02",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "\\frac{\\text{d}N}{\\text{d}t}=-k(200-N)"
            }
          ],
          ":answer-field/correct": [
            ":answer/id",
            "1590d796-ddbb-5261-9314-57adf67575fa"
          ]
        }
      ],
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The rate of change is proportional to the difference between the maximum capacity and the current population. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}N}{\\text{d}t}=k(a-N),\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ is the maximum capacity and $k>0$.\n\nHere $a=200$ deer, so\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}N}{\\text{d}t}=k(200-N).\n$$"
    },
